{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 12, "model_name": "qwen/qwen3.5-397b-a17b", "content": "Arthur woke to the familiar chirp of his alarm, but as he reached out to silence it, his hand passed directly through the plastic casing, triggering a floating menu that asked if he wanted to \"Adjust Volume\" or \"Skip Morning Sequence.\" Panic surged through him, yet it felt oddly muted, like an emotion rendered with low-resolution textures. He stumbled out of bed, expecting the creak of old floorboards, but his feet made a soft, looping thud sound that repeated identically with every step, and when he looked in the mirror, he saw a faint, shimmering polygon count hovering over his reflection instead of his usual tired eyes.\n\n***\n\nRushing outside, the world revealed its true nature; the clouds moved in rigid, pre-programmed loops, and the neighbors stood frozen in T-poses until he walked within a specific radius, at which point they snapped into animated greetings with delayed lip-syncing. Arthur tried to scream for help, but a dialogue box appeared before his mouth could open, offering three distinct choices for how to react to the beautiful morning, none of which allowed him to express his terror. He realized with sinking dread that he was no longer the player controlling the character, but the character himself, trapped in a save file where the only way out was to find a glitch in the code or wait for someone on the other side of the screen to finally press quit.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Arthur", "logprob": -0.00046299683}, {"token": " woke", "logprob": -0.0016746827}, {"token": " to", "logprob": -0.0011355169}, {"token": " the", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " familiar", "logprob": -0.0021293168}, {"token": " chir", "logprob": -0.04286662}, {"token": "p", "logprob": -0.6931472}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " his", "logprob": -1.192093e-07}, {"token": " alarm", "logprob": -0.033061568}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.0067153242}, {"to